Subject: [PATCH 2/2] U19 review: doors that open as menus behave like the
 links they replaced

About, Topics, and Family were plain links or did not exist before
2026-10-26; as menus they lost three things a reader had:

- Desktop: a mouse that hovered a door and then clicked it folded the
  menu the hover had just opened (About most of all, which used to be a
  link). The click after a hover now keeps it open; a second click, or
  Enter from the keyboard, toggles as before.
- Desktop: the door holding the page in view reads as current
  (mustard-text and aria-current), by the longest matching header link,
  so /resources/creeds is Study and /books is About.
- Phone: the whole row of a door is its toggle, not only the chevron at
  the right edge; rows keep their 48px rhythm.

Three tests in siteNav.test.tsx, each failing without its fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
